ia] during the gold rush\"\n\nFrom Paragraph 42: \"Black Hill, Victoria... named after the major landmark, Black Hill, on which there was extensive and highly profitable open-cut gold mining from the early 1850s during the Victoria gold rush.\"\n\nFrom Paragraph 55: Melbourne \"served as the major port... during the Gold Rush era.\"\n\nFrom Paragraph 114 (Otto Binswanger) - mentions Virginia, Norway, Oslo, and Switzerland going back and forth.\n\nWait, let me think about this more carefully. The question is asking:\n- What shares a border with the city where [a person] works?\n- That person went to [a state] during the gold rush\n- That state is where planes were originally going on 9/11\n\nActually, let me re-read Paragraph 10 again about 9/11:\n\"four airliners all bound for California\"\n\nSo the state = California.\n\nThat's a lot of searching - I should try a more systematic approach with the grep tool. Let me search for specific clues.","time":{"start":1777650467779,"end":1777650467779}}}
