aybe the answer is related to Oak Lawn sharing a border with Chicago.\n\nActually, going back to the first search, I found: **Oak Lawn shares borders with Chicago** (Paragraph 27).\n\nBut I need to complete the chain first. Let me re-examine the question logic:\n\n1. Planes went to California on 9/11\n2. During the gold rush, a person went to California\n3. That person works in the Gold Rush era (Paragraph 114) during the Gold Rush, Melbourne served as the major port and provided most services for the region...\")\n\nThen I need to find the city where this person works, and what shares a border with it.\n\nLooking at all the gold rush related documents:\n- Paragraph 4: California Gold Rush - Samuel Brannan\n- Paragraph 51: Black Hill, Victoria - Australia gold rush, William Urquhart\n- Paragraph 114: Melbourne - Victorian gold rush\n- Paragraph 172: Klondike Gold Rush - Yukon, Canada\n\nI'm trying to connect these to find the answer.","time":{"start":1777650507066,"end":1777650507066}}}
