the correct chain through the multi-hop question. Let me provide a good summary.\n</think>\n\n---\n## Goal\n\nThe user is trying to solve a multi-hop research question: \"What shares a border with the city where the person who went to the state where the planes were originally going on 9/11 during the gold rush works?\" This requires tracing a chain of connections across multiple pieces of information in the provided documents.\n\n## Instructions\n\n- Use the read and grep tools to search through documents\n- Base the answer ONLY on information found in the documents\n- Do not guess or use own knowledge\n- Output final answer on its own line: ANSWER: <your answer>\n\nThe key challenge is correctly parsing the multi-hop chain and connecting the information properly.\n\n## Discoveries\n\nFound these key connections:\n- **9/11 planes were originally going to California** (all four hijacked planes were said to be \"bound for California\")\n- **California Gold Rush** involved newspaper publisher/merchant **Samuel Brannan** who walked through San Francisco with gold\n- **San Francisco** is the city mentioned in the context of the California Gold Rush (Paragraph 4)\n- **Oak Lawn shares borders with Chicago** (Paragraph 2) - but this doesn't directly connect\n- **Melbourne** is mentioned twice: (1) Australian Victorian gold rush city (Paragraph 11), (2) near Mount Olive in Arkansas (Paragraph 90)\n- Border mentions found: Oak Lawn/Chicago, Virginia Honduras/El Salvador, Mount Bosworth (Alberta/British Columbia), Biysky District\n- No direct border information for San Francisco found in documents\n\nThe parsing challenge is that \"during the gold rush\" could modify: (1) the state event, or (2) the person's travel.\n\n## Accomplished\n\n- Read the complete prompt file (98 paragraphs of documents)\n- Identified planes were bound for California on 9/11\n- Traced California Gold Rush connections to Samuel Brannan and San Francisco\n- Searched for border information in the docum